      "title": "Of big fish and small genomes. Ocean sunfish shines.",
      "abstract": "<jats:p>**Deep (ocean) sequencing. Big-(fish) data. **The ocean sunfish, must officially be one of the world's weirdest creatures to enter the \"genome club\", and have its genetic code mapped. Laying the most eggs of any other known vertebrate (up to 300,000,000 at a time), and starting out as the size of the head of a pin, sunfish grow to become to largest bony fish in the sea.</jats:p>",
